        <div class="fc-delta-reason">IAEA DG Grossi stated on June 26 that the MOU includes IAEA access to Iranian nuclear facilities and that inspections "will happen." Iran's deputy FM Gharibabadi contradicted this on June 25, stating there are "no plans" for inspector access before a final deal. Iran's MFA spokesman Baghaei confirmed no schedule for IAEA visits. The June 26 US-Iran military exchange further complicated any near-term inspection arrangement. p=0.30 reflects Iran's stated blocking position against Grossi's public assertion and the MOU text pressure.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if the IAEA publicly confirms in a press release or DG statement that inspectors have physically entered at least one Iranian nuclear facility for monitoring or verification purposes before EOD 2026-07-15.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>IAEA official press release or DG statement, corroborated by Reuters, AP, or AFP.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Requests for access, scheduling discussions, or diplomatic contacts without confirmed physical entry = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO; access without official IAEA framing it as a monitoring visit = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
